    "note": "**Put off** and **postpone** both mean deciding to do something later; **postpone** is more formal and usual for official events (*The game was postponed*), while **put off** is everyday (*I keep putting off my homework*). **Delay** often means that something happens later than planned without anyone deciding it (*The train was delayed*)."
  },
